@startuml
!include style.iuml
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
title Scenario - preview, consent, and a name collision
autonumber
participant "Dowlume\n(domain boundary)" as Dowlume
participant "Organization\nPolicy" as Policy
participant "Downloaded File\nreport.pdf" as File
participant Preview
participant "Operation\norganizeReport" as Operation
[-> Dowlume : request Preview for selected folder
Dowlume -> File : observe eligibility, readiness, and content
File --> Dowlume : eligible; ready; fingerprint H-report
Dowlume -> Policy : classify report.pdf
Policy --> Dowlume : Documents; category folder Documents
Dowlume -> Dowlume : observe Documents/report.pdf already occupied
Dowlume -> Preview : retain proposal: Documents/report (1).pdf\nand fingerprint H-report
Dowlume -->[ : show proposed destination; no file moved
[-> Dowlume : accept Organize and monitor\nfor the unchanged policy
Dowlume -> File : recheck readiness and observed content
alt content still matches
  Dowlume -> Dowlume : re-evaluate destination availability
  create Operation
  Dowlume -> Operation : record Pending Organize\nwith source and intended after facts
  Dowlume -> File : move to available Documents/report (1).pdf\nwithout replacing existing content
  File --> Dowlume : move verified
  Dowlume -> Operation : confirm Completed and resulting file facts
  Dowlume -->[ : show Organized; begin monitoring\nafter all preview items are processed
else content changed after Preview
  Dowlume -->[ : reject stale proposal; request fresh Preview
  note over File, Operation
    No Organize Operation is recorded for the rejected proposal.
    The source and the existing destination remain untouched.
  end note
end
legend bottom
  A conceptual scenario: messages express domain observations and commitments, not C# calls.
  The occupied name is unchanged throughout this example. A new collision would select another suffix.
  Recovery of earlier operations precedes candidate preview and is omitted here.
endlegend
@enduml
